<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Zapotec Kingdom of Tehuantepec</h1><p class="st-meta">1490 CE – 1521 CE (approx.) · capital Tehuantepec</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last independent Zapotec kingdom, on the Isthmus of Tehuantepec, which withstood an Aztec siege at the fortress of Guiengola.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the late 15th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zapotec-civilization">Zapotec</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cocijoeza">Cocijoeza</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zaachila">Zaachila</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isthmus-of-tehuantepec">Isthmus of Tehuantepec</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixe">Mixe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoque">Zoque</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huave">Huave</a> peoples and moved his royal seat there, around 1490, gaining control of the trade route between central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xoconusco">Soconusco</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahuitzotl">Ahuitzotl</a> sought to seize the isthmus, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cocijoeza">Cocijoeza</a> held out at the mountain fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guiengola">Guiengola</a> in a long siege in the late 1490s. Peace was sealed by his marriage to an Aztec princess, and their son Cocijopii succeeded him. The kingdom ruled a mixed population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zapotecs">Zapotecs</a> and other peoples in a rich lowland.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Cocijopii submitted to the Spanish around 1521 and was baptised Juan Cortés Cocijopii, keeping noble rank. Tehuantepec became a colonial town within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/new-spain">New Spain</a>, and the isthmus remains a stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zapotec-civilization">Zapotec</a> culture.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1490 CE – 1521 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.35%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1490 CE – 1521 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tehuantepec</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cocijoeza, Cocijopii</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Zapotec religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Zapotec</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tehuantepec</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1506&amp;focus=zapotec-kingdom-of-tehuantepec" aria-label="Zapotec Kingdom of Tehuantepec on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="1883 1485 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Zapotec Kingdom of Tehuantepec lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2203 1741L2368 1804M2203 1741L2321 1717"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2368 1804h0M2321 1717h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2203 1741h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2203 1741h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tehuantepec. <a href="/atlas?year=1506&amp;focus=zapotec-kingdom-of-tehuantepec">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
